Chapter: Maybe

 A Maybe is one of Just carrying a value, or None.
 To from-maybe gives the value inside Just, or the default when the Maybe is None.
 To is-just gives True when the Maybe is Just, False otherwise.
 To is-none gives True when the Maybe is None, False otherwise.
 To maybe-map gives Just of the function applied to the value when Just, or None when None.
 To maybe-bind gives the result of the function applied to the value when Just, or None when None.

 We say:

Section: Definitions

  Maybe (a) =
    | Just (a)
    | None

  from-maybe : Maybe a, a -> a
  from-maybe (m) (default) = when m
    is Just (x) -> x
    is None -> default

  is-just : Maybe a -> Boolean
  is-just (m) = when m
    is Just (x) -> True
    is None -> False

  is-none : Maybe a -> Boolean
  is-none (m) = when m
    is Just (x) -> False
    is None -> True

  maybe-map : (a -> b), Maybe a -> Maybe b
  maybe-map (f) (m) = when m
    is Just (x) -> Just (f x)
    is None -> None

  maybe-bind : Maybe a, (a -> Maybe b) -> Maybe b
  maybe-bind (m) (f) = when m
    is Just (x) -> f x
    is None -> None

